  "generated_text": "1. The diameter of the sphere is equal to the edge length of the cube.\n2. Since the edge length of the cube is 6 inches, the diameter of the sphere is also 6 inches.\n3. The radius of the sphere is half of the diameter, so the radius is \\( \\frac{6}{2} = 3 \\) inches.\n4. The volume \\( V \\) of a sphere is given by the formula \\( V = \\frac{4}{3} \\pi r^3 \\).\n5. Substitute the radius \\( r = 3 \\) inches into the formula:\n   \\[\n   V = \\frac{4}{3} \\pi (3)^3\n   \\]\n6. Calculate \\( (3)^3 \\):\n   \\[\n   (3)^3 = 27\n   \\]\n7. Substitute back into the formula:\n   \\[\n   V = \\frac{4}{3} \\pi \\times 27\n   \\]\n8. Simplify the expression:\n   \\[\n   V = 36\\pi\n   \\]\n\nTherefore, the volume of the sphere is \\(\\boxed{36\\pi}\\).",
  "grade": {
    "error": null,
    "extracted_answer": "[36*pi, '36\\\\pi']",
    "gold_answer": "[asy]\nsize(70);\ndraw(Circle((6,6),4.5));\ndraw((10.5,6)..(6,6.9)..(1.5,6),linetype(\"2 4\"));\ndraw((10.5,6)..(6,5.1)..(1.5,6));\ndraw((0,0)--(9,0)--(9,9)--(0,9)--cycle);\ndraw((0,9)--(3,12)--(12,12)--(9,9));\ndraw((12,12)--(12,3)--(9,0));\ndraw((0,0)--(3,3)--(12,3),dashed); draw((3,3)--(3,12),dashed);\n[/asy] A sphere inscribed in a cube has diameter length equal to the side length of the cube.  Thus, the inscribed sphere has diameter 6 inches, radius $6/2=3$ inches, and volume \\[\\frac{4}{3}\\pi(3)^3=4\\cdot 3^2\\pi=\\boxed{36\\pi}\\] cubic inches.",
    "is_correct": true
  },
